
= Project Time Management

== Activity
Activity is the element of work normally found on Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) that has an expected duration, cost and resource requirements. Activities are the building blocks of a project and are used to define the work that needs to be completed in order to achieve the project objectives. Each activity should be clearly defined, measurable, and achievable within a specific timeframe.\

Activity Definitation involves developing a more detailed WBS and supporting explanations to understand all the work to be done, so you can develop realistic cost and duration estimates.

=== Decomposition of Activities
+ Sub divide work packages into schedule activities.
+ Define activities to meet project objectives.
+ Activities should be relatively small and manageable.
+ Activities may be work packages or lower level items.
+ WBS and Activity list may be developed sequentially or in parallel.

=== Activity Sequencing
Activity sequencing is the process of identifying and documenting relationships among the project activities. It involves determining the
order in which activities will be performed and how they are related to one another. This process helps to create a logical flow of work and ensures that dependencies between activities are properly managed.

== Network Diagram
A network diagram is a graphical representation for showing activity sequencing. It is a schematic display of the logical relationship among the project schedule activities. It is used to visualize the sequence of activities and their dependencies, which helps in planning and managing the project schedule effectively.

== Precedence Diagramming Method (PDM)
The Precedence Diagramming Method (PDM) is a technique used to construct a project schedule network diagram that uses boxes or nodes to represent activities and connects them with arrows to show the dependencies between the activities. PDM is widely used in project management because it provides a clear and visual representation of the project schedule, making it easier to understand and communicate the relationships between activities.


